{"result": {"url": "https://openbooks.net/books/stochastic-governance", "title": "Stochastic Governance — MIT Policy Press", "text": "Publisher page. Stochastic Governance: Probabilistic Approaches to Policy Design Under Uncertainty by Vasilis Papadimitriou and Sakura Nishihara. MIT Policy Press, 2021. Hardcover, 312 pages. ISBN: 978-0-26203-847-1.

Conventional policy analysis is built for a world of knowable futures. Stochastic Governance proposes a new framework for policy design under deep uncertainty: adaptive policy envelopes that encode commitment distributions rather than fixed prescriptions, allowing policy to respond to evidence without sacrificing credibility. Three case studies: Netherlands coastal infrastructure, pandemic response protocol design, long-term infrastructure investment under seismic risk.

Endorsement: 'The most important contribution to policy design theory in a decade.' — Professor A. van der Berg, Delft University of Technology."}, "actions": [], "error": null}
